  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolian businesses face significant difficulties integrating into regional trade and investment networks because many enterprises still lack sufficient knowledge and practical capacity to implement labour standards, among other things, making it harder for them to meet the compliance expectations of international markets; at the same time, employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs) struggle with gaps in the member services required to provide this knowledge, particularly technical guidance on labour standards, ESG principles, and responsible business conduct, which limits their ability to support enterprises in aligning with global norms and thereby weakens the overall competitiveness of the business community.
          In response, the Mongolian National Chamber of Commerce and Industry (MNCCI) and Mongolian Employers Confederation (MONEF) will expand targeted support to help enterprises understand and apply international labour standards, ESG principles, and responsible business conduct. At the same time, ongoing national-level reforms require national EBMOs to strengthen their capacity to engage effectively in labour-market institutions and related policy dialogue, ensuring that business perspectives - including issues related to gender equality and women in business and management - are well represented as the regulatory environment evolves.
          Expected result: Employers and business membership organizations in Mongolia become more responsive and resilient by adapting their organizational structures and developing new or enhanced services that better align with the evolving needs of their members.</narrative>
  </description>
